{
  "description": "Layer-resolved routing concentration, in response to Reviewer 1. Pooling expert activations over MoE layers understates the concentration present in any single layer, because different layers concentrate on different experts and cancel.",
  "decoder_caveat": "For seq2seq models (Switch) the decoder MoE layers are excluded. We run a single forward pass to read the router and there is no generation task, so the decoder receives one start token per sequence. Its layers therefore see ~2% of the activations of an encoder layer and trivially send them to a single expert. That is not specialization, and reporting it as such would be wrong.",
